 "state_profile": {
  "voting_summary": "California mails every registered voter a ballot, and 78% of its 2024 vote came by mail, with ballots postmarked by election day accepted for a week afterward. Early voting is available in most counties, but the share is small and often inseparable between mail and election day reports. Polls close at 11 p.m. Eastern; pre-processed mail is released first, election day precincts follow overnight, and late mail is verified in batches over the following weeks. Mail ran D+27 versus R+3 on election day, so the state drifts steadily bluer through the canvass.",
